The -p text path no longer prints a partial answer twice when yoagent retries internally on a pipe. It's committed as eaeab54f. The full test suite passes (6254 tests, 0 failed), and clippy with -D warnings and cargo fmt --check are clean.

Before the fix: I ran the two ignored #989 tests exactly as written. Both failed the same way:

```
PROBE #987: stdout="PARTIAL_\n\nPONG\n" success=true requests=2
left: "PARTIAL_\n\nPONG\n"   right: "PARTIAL_\n"
```

The change (`src/prompt.rs`):
• yoagent's retry event (ProviderRetry) is now handled explicitly instead of being dropped. A new field, attempt_text_start, marks where the current message's text begins in collected_text, so the code can tell what the failing attempt already streamed.
• It reuses the Day-216 check (retry_blocked_by_streamed_partial) and the same stderr note. There's no second copy of either.
• **Retry blocked** (stdout is a pipe and text already streamed): it prints the error and the note to stderr, marks the turn fatal, and stops the agent. The `Aborted stop that follows is ignored by classify_stop_reason`, so it can't overwrite the error, and the process exits non-zero.
• **Retry allowed** (no text yet, a terminal, or `--print`/json, which hold stdout back): yoagent retries as before, and the failed attempt's text is removed from the collected answer.

After the fix:
• I un-ignored both #989 tests without editing their assertions. Both pass: stdout is "PARTIAL_\n", one request, non-zero exit.
• The case where the retry works, a 429 before any text, still gives exactly PONG\n, exit 0 and 2 requests.
• Positive control, run as one command: with the new code disabled (marked NEUTERED), exactly the two #989 tests fail by name. After restoring it, all three pass, and no marker is left in the source.

Two count checks raised on purpose:
• `every_retry_site_consults_the_shared_rule` now expects 5 sites instead of 4. The fifth is yoagent's own retry.
• `every_streamed_text_write_is_gated now expects 15 instead of 14. The new code writes through the gated write_stream_text`.

These tests use exact counts so that anyone adding a site has to decide about it. Each bump has a comment saying why.

Known gap: the fix only works if the agent is stopped while yoagent is waiting before its second attempt. These errors don't carry a Retry-After header, so the wait defaults to 1 second and the stop arrives in time. If a provider sent a partial answer followed by Retry-After: 0, the second request could go out first. No test covers that case; it's written down in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Not done (out of scope): the stream-json event loop, which is Task 2. #989 stays open. ARCHITECTURE.md has a new Day 219 entry under the src/prompt.rs notes describing this change and saying the stream-json path is handled separately.
